1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,990
20 minutes ago this game didn't exist.

2
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:07,120
My daughter drew it on two cards.

3
00:00:11,210 --> 00:00:15,410
Hello, I'm Grzegorz.
I'm from Gdańsk, Poland.

4
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:17,520
I would like to show you Diorama.

5
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:23,400
What is Diorama? Diorama lets you to build
a world, a world you can interact with

6
00:00:23,450 --> 00:00:28,150
and play it as a game, as
a point-and-click game.

7
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:34,680
Those cards are drawn by my daughter.

8
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:39,060
First picture, picture,

9
00:00:40,430 --> 00:00:47,170
Take a photo.
So make me a nice game out of this.

10
00:00:47,390 --> 00:00:50,750
So let's click build.
This is the Winky cat.

11
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:54,230
Okay, the llama, Banana Bob.

12
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:59,880
From here Diorama builds it all.

13
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:05,420
The story, the painted places, the
cutouts, the character and their voices.

14
00:01:09,130 --> 00:01:17,030
You can see here that using SAM we were
able to actually select some objects.

15
00:01:17,130 --> 00:01:23,190
So for this one we have the Muse Image
had to generate front, back, side,

16
00:01:24,070 --> 00:01:27,810
other side as well. And now
we have the model actually.

17
00:01:27,930 --> 00:01:30,830
It's very nice.
Ah, you can see here the depth.

18
00:01:31,190 --> 00:01:34,400
So depth is important for various reasons.

19
00:01:34,450 --> 00:01:38,220
We are using it for walking, but
not only for various visual effects.

20
00:01:38,270 --> 00:01:43,240
So checks is also an important part because
the workflow is actually trying to play

21
00:01:43,290 --> 00:01:47,010
the game, whether it's possible to click
through things, walk through the world.

22
00:01:57,010 --> 00:01:58,810
Ooh, shiny! I'll keep it safe.

23
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:03,510
Oh, hello, little friend.

24
00:02:04,030 --> 00:02:06,950
I'm Winky. The sunny
hill is too quiet today.

25
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:08,550
Will you help me?

26
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:16,060
And let's make a prompt. I
will say I want this cat.

27
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:24,760
Make this cat house yellow.

28
00:02:31,350 --> 00:02:35,180
All the objects you can see in this game
were actually hand drawn by the children

29
00:02:35,230 --> 00:02:39,230
and not inside detail. It's very nice.

30
00:02:39,410 --> 00:02:44,950
I recommend Diorama. Thanks for
watching and enjoy your day.

31
00:02:45,370 --> 00:02:49,990
A few drawings and one sentence,
a game you can play and share.

32
00:02:50,230 --> 00:02:51,490
That's Diorama.
